# Docker build-context excludes. Keep this lean: the context is sent to the daemon before
# `turbo prune` runs, so trimming build artifacts + deps speeds every image build.
#
# IMPORTANT: this must NOT exclude the committed chain manifest
# (packages/chain/src/deployments/97.json) or the codegen'd deployments.generated.ts —
# images MUST build from the committed manifest, never a zero/stale one. They live under
# packages/chain/src (never matched below), so no negation is required; documented here so a
# future broad `packages/**/generated` rule doesn't silently drop them.

# Dependencies — reinstalled in the builder via `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`
**/node_modules

# Build outputs — regenerated in the builder
**/.next
**/dist
**/.turbo
.turbo

# Contracts / Hardhat artifacts — not needed by any app image
packages/contracts/artifacts
packages/contracts/cache
packages/contracts/types
packages/contracts/ignition/deployments

# Test + coverage output
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/.playwright

# Local env + secrets — never bake into an image (runtime-only)
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Editor / OS / VCS noise
.git
.github
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log

# Docs + planning (not needed at build time) — EXCEPT the public, secret-free files the docs-site
# prebuild mirrors into its Reference section (apps/docs/scripts/sync-reference-docs.mjs). Keep this
# allowlist in sync with that script's ALLOWLIST. Internal docs (code-review, *-runbook, brainstorms,
# plans, reviews, solutions) stay excluded so they never enter the build context.
docs
!docs/architecture.md
!docs/routing.md
!docs/threat-model.md
